steps.thought:
We need to look at the actual bug: The issue is that when a proxy responds with 401 WWW-Authenticate instead of 407 Proxy-Authenticate, libcurl incorrectly treats it as proxy auth and sends credentials to the proxy. In the function inspecting tunnel response, they had logic to handle both 401 and 407, but they should only treat 407 as proxy auth. The code we saw had:

if(resp->status == 401) {
    auth_reply = Curl_dynhds_cget(&resp->headers, "WWW-Authenticate");
}
else if(resp->status == 407) {
    auth_reply = Curl_dynhds_cget(&resp->headers, "Proxy-Authenticate");
}

That would cause a 401 to be treated as proxy auth (WWW-Authenticate) and then later used to authenticate to the proxy (wro

